Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:01.05,Talk,,0,0,0,,Hello everyone.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:01.05,0:00:03.64,Talk,,0,0,0,,Today, I will be presenting LaGarNet:
Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.64,0:00:09.39,Talk,,0,0,0,,a latent world model designed for quasi-static,\Npick-and-place garment flattening.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.39,0:00:15.13,Talk,,0,0,0,,We show that a single policy trained\Nentirely in simulation flattens four distinct
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.13,0:00:17.30,Talk,,0,0,0,,garment types on real hardware,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.30,0:00:19.27,Talk,,0,0,0,,with no further fine-tuning.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.62,0:00:22.38,Talk,,0,0,0,,Our primary task is garment flattening,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.38,0:00:28.12,Talk,,0,0,0,,a critical prerequisite for downstream\Ntasks like folding, ironing, and pressing.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.12,0:00:34.08,Talk,,0,0,0,,This task is inherently challenging because\Ncloth possesses vast degrees of freedom,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.08,0:00:36.99,Talk,,0,0,0,,undergoes severe non-linear deformations,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:36.99,0:00:41.31,Talk,,0,0,0,,and exhibits high self-occlusion\Nfrom a top-down perspective.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.31,0:00:47.27,Talk,,0,0,0,,To rigorously evaluate the underlying\Nrepresentation rather than relying on hardware
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.27,0:00:48.04,Talk,,0,0,0,,complexity,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:48.04,0:00:52.94,Talk,,0,0,0,,we deliberately constrain our physical\Nsetup to a single robotic arm,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.94,0:00:57.40,Talk,,0,0,0,,a single pick-and-place primitive,\Nand one top-down RGB camera.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:57.75,0:01:02.32,Talk,,0,0,0,,Existing data-driven flatteners\Ngenerally fall into three families.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:02.32,0:01:05.73,Talk,,0,0,0,,Behaviour cloning is\Nconceptually straightforward,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.73,0:01:11.39,Talk,,0,0,0,,but adequately covering the vast state\Nspace of crumpled configurations requires an
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.39,0:01:14.32,Talk,,0,0,0,,impractical volume of\Nhuman demonstrations,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:14.32,0:01:16.85,Talk,,0,0,0,,often necessitating scripted oracles.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.85,0:01:21.14,Talk,,0,0,0,,Model-free reinforcement learning\Nexplores this space directly,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:21.14,0:01:23.05,Talk,,0,0,0,,yielding general flatteners,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:23.05,0:01:28.58,Talk,,0,0,0,,but suffers from poor sample efficiency\Nand cannot predict the forward effects of
Dialogue: 0,0:01:28.58,0:01:29.12,Talk,,0,0,0,,actions.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:29.12,0:01:32.94,Talk,,0,0,0,,Model-based methods remain\Nrare in garment manipulation;
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.94,0:01:38.12,Talk,,0,0,0,,standard latent models tend to produce\Nblurred reconstructions that lose the
Dialogue: 0,0:01:38.12,0:01:41.94,Talk,,0,0,0,,critical edge and corner\Nfeatures necessary for shaping.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:41.94,0:01:44.74,Talk,,0,0,0,,This leads to our core research question:
Dialogue: 0,0:01:44.74,0:01:50.40,Talk,,0,0,0,,can latent world models built for continuous\Ncontrol still function in quasi-static
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.40,0:01:51.56,Talk,,0,0,0,,primitive setups,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:51.56,0:01:55.72,Talk,,0,0,0,,where consecutive observations\Nare not temporally continuous?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:56.07,0:02:01.85,Talk,,0,0,0,,Our solution is LaGarNet, built upon a\Ngoal-conditioned recurrent state-space model.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:01.85,0:02:07.43,Talk,,0,0,0,,The fundamental design choice here is the\Ndirect integration of goal-conditioning
Dialogue: 0,0:02:07.43,0:02:10.25,Talk,,0,0,0,,into the latent inference process itself.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:10.25,0:02:15.69,Talk,,0,0,0,,Both the prior and posterior distributions\Nover the latent state are explicitly
Dialogue: 0,0:02:15.69,0:02:16.45,Talk,,0,0,0,,goal-aware.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:16.45,0:02:21.82,Talk,,0,0,0,,A recurrent backbone maintains a belief\Nstate over the occluded regions of the
Dialogue: 0,0:02:21.82,0:02:22.37,Talk,,0,0,0,,garment,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:22.37,0:02:27.46,Talk,,0,0,0,,while a joint decoder predicts both\Nthe top-down mask and the task reward.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:27.46,0:02:31.39,Talk,,0,0,0,,During inference, we plan\Nusing the cross-entropy method,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:31.39,0:02:36.96,Talk,,0,0,0,,sampling candidate pick-and-place actions\Nand ranking them based on the predicted
Dialogue: 0,0:02:36.96,0:02:37.44,Talk,,0,0,0,,reward.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:37.44,0:02:43.02,Talk,,0,0,0,,Ablation studies reveal that removing\Ngoal-conditioning from the latent inference
Dialogue: 0,0:02:43.02,0:02:47.29,Talk,,0,0,0,,costs twenty-two and a half\Npercentage points of success rate,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:47.29,0:02:51.08,Talk,,0,0,0,,from seventy-five percent\Ndown to fifty-two and a half.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:51.43,0:02:55.15,Talk,,0,0,0,,Our second contribution is\Nthe data collection paradigm.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:55.15,0:02:59.80,Talk,,0,0,0,,We train a Diffusion Policy expert\Non just fifty human demonstrations,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:59.80,0:03:05.39,Talk,,0,0,0,,allowing it to reliably reach near-flattened\Nstates that a random exploration policy
Dialogue: 0,0:03:05.39,0:03:06.85,Talk,,0,0,0,,would rarely discover.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:06.85,0:03:12.30,Talk,,0,0,0,,We then mix this expert's rollouts in a\None-to-one ratio with a mask-biased random
Dialogue: 0,0:03:12.30,0:03:12.76,Talk,,0,0,0,,policy,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:12.76,0:03:18.15,Talk,,0,0,0,,which drives state exploration by uniformly\Nsampling pick points exclusively from
Dialogue: 0,0:03:18.15,0:03:20.28,Talk,,0,0,0,,the garment's segmentation mask.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:20.28,0:03:25.73,Talk,,0,0,0,,This approach yields a robust dataset of\Nfive thousand episodes without relying on
Dialogue: 0,0:03:25.73,0:03:27.39,Talk,,0,0,0,,complex scripted oracles,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:27.39,0:03:32.84,Talk,,0,0,0,,creating a paradigm that is agnostic to\Ncloth dynamics and likely to generalise to
Dialogue: 0,0:03:32.84,0:03:34.83,Talk,,0,0,0,,other deformable object tasks.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:35.18,0:03:39.59,Talk,,0,0,0,,Our third contribution is a\Nnovel coverage-alignment reward.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:39.59,0:03:43.92,Talk,,0,0,0,,This metric jointly evaluates\Nstate coverage and alignment,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:43.92,0:03:48.18,Talk,,0,0,0,,computed entirely from top-down\Nbinary segmentation masks.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:48.18,0:03:48.91,Talk,,0,0,0,,Crucially,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:48.91,0:03:54.79,Talk,,0,0,0,,it eliminates the need for privileged\Nparticle-level state or learned smoothness
Dialogue: 0,0:03:54.79,0:03:55.59,Talk,,0,0,0,,estimators.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:55.59,0:04:01.59,Talk,,0,0,0,,This allows the exact same continuous and\Nlinear reward function to be evaluated in
Dialogue: 0,0:04:01.69,0:04:04.99,Talk,,0,0,0,,simulation and directly\Non physical hardware,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.99,0:04:08.59,Talk,,0,0,0,,making it highly amenable\Nto predictive learning.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:08.94,0:04:12.31,Talk,,0,0,0,,In simulation, LaGarNet\Nachieves parity with MEDOR,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:12.31,0:04:14.96,Talk,,0,0,0,,the state-of-the-art mesh-based planner,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:14.96,0:04:20.25,Talk,,0,0,0,,whilst outperforming both PlaNet-ClothPick\Nand Diffusion Policy across short and
Dialogue: 0,0:04:20.25,0:04:21.90,Talk,,0,0,0,,medium planning horizons.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:21.90,0:04:23.36,Talk,,0,0,0,,Furthermore, a single,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:23.36,0:04:27.79,Talk,,0,0,0,,unified policy trained across all\Ngarments outperforms specialised,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:27.79,0:04:29.37,Talk,,0,0,0,,single-garment variants,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:29.37,0:04:34.20,Talk,,0,0,0,,suggesting that morphological diversity\Nacts as a beneficial regulariser.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:34.20,0:04:34.93,Talk,,0,0,0,,Ultimately,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:34.93,0:04:40.48,Talk,,0,0,0,,the policy exceeds ninety-five percent\Nnormalised coverage across all four simulated
Dialogue: 0,0:04:40.48,0:04:43.53,Talk,,0,0,0,,garment categories within\Ntwenty action steps.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:43.88,0:04:47.90,Talk,,0,0,0,,This comparison also has a\Ncrucial computational dimension.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:47.90,0:04:53.49,Talk,,0,0,0,,LaGarNet requires five times fewer parameters\Nthan MEDOR and plans seventeen times
Dialogue: 0,0:04:53.49,0:04:53.97,Talk,,0,0,0,,faster,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:53.97,0:04:56.36,Talk,,0,0,0,,with no loss in flattening quality.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:56.36,0:05:01.06,Talk,,0,0,0,,Six seconds of planning per action\Nis affordable on a physical robot,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:01.06,0:05:03.99,Talk,,0,0,0,,where one hundred and\Nthree seconds is not.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:03.99,0:05:09.65,Talk,,0,0,0,,We are careful not to overstate this: with\Nperception and robot execution included,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:09.65,0:05:14.43,Talk,,0,0,0,,a single real manipulation step still\Ntakes about twenty-four seconds,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:14.43,0:05:19.20,Talk,,0,0,0,,so the full perception-action cycle\Nremains the deployment bottleneck.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:19.55,0:05:25.23,Talk,,0,0,0,,We subsequently transferred this\Nsimulation-trained policy directly to a physical
Dialogue: 0,0:05:25.23,0:05:26.42,Talk,,0,0,0,,UR5e robotic arm,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:26.42,0:05:29.79,Talk,,0,0,0,,achieving this with zero\Nreal-world fine-tuning.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:29.79,0:05:34.63,Talk,,0,0,0,,The videos shown here demonstrate\Nrollouts on all four garment types,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:34.63,0:05:37.15,Talk,,0,0,0,,accelerated to ten times real speed.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:37.15,0:05:42.20,Talk,,0,0,0,,The policy operates solely on a\Ntop-down observation and the goal image,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:42.20,0:05:47.60,Talk,,0,0,0,,and the reward is computed from the\Nexact same segmentation masks utilised in
Dialogue: 0,0:05:47.60,0:05:48.37,Talk,,0,0,0,,simulation.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.37,0:05:53.98,Talk,,0,0,0,,This consistency is precisely what enables\Nsuccessful zero-shot transfer without
Dialogue: 0,0:05:53.98,0:05:58.12,Talk,,0,0,0,,requiring a highly tuned digital\Ntwin of the physical cell.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:58.47,0:06:03.88,Talk,,0,0,0,,Quantitatively, across forty physical\Ntrials of twenty actions each,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:03.88,0:06:09.06,Talk,,0,0,0,,LaGarNet achieves ninety point\Nthree percent normalised coverage,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:09.06,0:06:13.04,Talk,,0,0,0,,eighty point seven percent\Nnormalised improvement,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:13.04,0:06:18.45,Talk,,0,0,0,,and an eighty-one point one percent\Nmaximum intersection over union.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:18.45,0:06:23.15,Talk,,0,0,0,,It successfully completes\Ntwenty-seven out of forty trials,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:23.15,0:06:27.93,Talk,,0,0,0,,against nine out of forty for\Nthe PlaNet-ClothPick baseline,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:27.93,0:06:33.02,Talk,,0,0,0,,though a human operator still\Nreaches thirty-eight out of forty.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:33.02,0:06:39.02,Talk,,0,0,0,,Success here means reaching eighty-five\Npercent coverage and seventy-five percent
Dialogue: 0,0:06:39.47,0:06:45.36,Talk,,0,0,0,,maximum intersection over union at any\Npoint within a twenty-step episode;
Dialogue: 0,0:06:45.36,0:06:51.36,Talk,,0,0,0,,we relax these thresholds from their\Nsimulation values to allow for the sim-to-real
Dialogue: 0,0:06:51.97,0:06:52.29,Talk,,0,0,0,,gap.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:52.29,0:06:55.32,Talk,,0,0,0,,We also stress-tested a fifth garment,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:55.32,0:07:01.32,Talk,,0,0,0,,a soft long-sleeved dress whose topology\Nis absent from the simulated training set.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:01.92,0:07:07.92,Talk,,0,0,0,,Evaluated separately over ten further\Ntrials, the policy recovers most of its area,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:08.53,0:07:14.34,Talk,,0,0,0,,at seventy-seven percent coverage,\Nbut never meets the success criterion,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:14.34,0:07:16.26,Talk,,0,0,0,,scoring zero out of ten.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:16.61,0:07:19.62,Talk,,0,0,0,,We draw two primary\Nlessons from this work.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:19.62,0:07:20.04,Talk,,0,0,0,,First,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:20.04,0:07:25.72,Talk,,0,0,0,,latent world models can be highly effective\Nin quasi-static manipulation regimes,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:25.72,0:07:31.33,Talk,,0,0,0,,provided that goal-conditioning is\Nintegrated directly into the latent inference
Dialogue: 0,0:07:31.33,0:07:31.89,Talk,,0,0,0,,process.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:31.89,0:07:36.44,Talk,,0,0,0,,Second, greedy, one-step planning\Nyields the highest performance.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:36.44,0:07:41.63,Talk,,0,0,0,,Because a single manipulation primitive\Ninduces massive state deformation,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:41.63,0:07:47.45,Talk,,0,0,0,,predictive error compounds faster than\Nextended lookahead can provide value—success
Dialogue: 0,0:07:47.45,0:07:51.65,Talk,,0,0,0,,drops from seventy-three point\Nthree percent at horizon one,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:51.65,0:07:54.04,Talk,,0,0,0,,to thirty percent at horizon five.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.04,0:07:59.79,Talk,,0,0,0,,The principal limitation of our current\Nsystem is the lack of an explicit stopping
Dialogue: 0,0:07:59.79,0:08:00.49,Talk,,0,0,0,,criterion.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:00.49,0:08:05.95,Talk,,0,0,0,,Immediate future work includes integrating\Na learned termination condition and
Dialogue: 0,0:08:05.95,0:08:09.39,Talk,,0,0,0,,extending the framework\Nto goal-directed folding.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:09.39,0:08:10.37,Talk,,0,0,0,,Looking ahead,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:10.37,0:08:15.98,Talk,,0,0,0,,we view this formulation as a promising\Npathway toward general deformable-object
Dialogue: 0,0:08:15.98,0:08:16.89,Talk,,0,0,0,,manipulation.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:16.89,0:08:18.57,Talk,,0,0,0,,Thank you for listening.
